<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="162" project="ebilling-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Accuracy and performance evaluation; tuning</title>
    <phase>7 Evaluation and rollout (WP7) — wave W7-2</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Measurement and configuration tuning (analyzer version, Action versions, settings) in dev; BFF code changes only if a defect is found, which then raises BFF hygiene.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Diagnosing extraction and coding misses and choosing tuning trade-offs (accuracy vs review load vs cost) is judgment-heavy, and missed targets go to the owner with options.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>005, 160, 161</deps>
    <tags>evaluation, ai, performance</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-4 days</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Measure eBilling against NFR-04 (extraction accuracy), NFR-05 (UTBMS task code top-1 at least 80%), NFR-06 (zero rejections from misread values) on the evaluation set, and NFR-01 (in-session result p90 at most 2 minutes) and NFR-02 (review page and panels p90 at most 3 s) in dev; tune — new analyzer version, new Action versions, settings from 161 — and re-measure; record results and an owner decision for any target still missed (FR-44).</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE AI engineer. Expert in Content Understanding analyzers, JPS Actions, evaluation methodology and performance measurement; disciplined about versioning every tuned artefact.</role>

  <goal>notes/evaluation-results.md reports baseline and tuned results per NFR with the artefact versions measured; every tuning change is a new version (analyzer sprk_invoice_vN, Action JPS version) or a recorded settings change; any target still missed has an owner decision recorded in notes/decisions-log.md.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-44, NFR-01 – NFR-06, success criteria 1, 2 and 8. Inputs: 005's extraction-spike.md and scoring harness (notes/spikes/); 161's calibration-report.md and harness (notes/calibration/) with recommended threshold, weights and caps; 160's coverage matrix (pipeline correct before tuning). Tunable artefacts: analyzer definition infrastructure/content-understanding/sprk-invoice-v1.json deployed by scripts/content-understanding/Deploy-Analyzers.ps1 (both from 004 — a changed definition is a new file sprk-invoice-v2.json; the script refuses a silent replace); Action mirrors infra/dataverse/actions/{invoice-classify,invoice-line-code,billing-rule-draft,invoice-firm-notice}.action.json seeded by scripts/Deploy-ActionMirrors.ps1 (a prompt change bumps the JPS version, which the correction record stores as sprk_sourceversion); sprk_ebillingsetting values (025) changed in dev through the admin form (audited, no deployment). Code-set mappings (048) and the coding chunk size (sprk_codingchunksize) also affect NFR-05 and NFR-01. NFR-02 surfaces: 110's review page, 106's context panel, 107's related work.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="output">projects/ebilling-r1/notes/evaluation-results.md</file>
      <file role="new">infrastructure/content-understanding/sprk-invoice-v2.json (only if the analyzer is tuned)</file>
      <file role="modify">infra/dataverse/actions/invoice-line-code.action.json and other eBilling Action mirrors (only if tuned; version bumped)</file>
      <file role="modify">projects/ebilling-r1/notes/decisions-log.md (owner decisions on missed targets)</file>
      <file role="read">projects/ebilling-r1/notes/calibration-report.md</file>
      <file role="read">projects/ebilling-r1/notes/extraction-spike.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="005" status="pending">Spike results, harness and go / no-go</dependency>
      <dependency task="160" status="pending">End-to-end correctness proven</dependency>
      <dependency task="161" status="pending">Calibration recommendations</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="D-81">Measure BOTH the preview primary analyzer and the GA fallback analyzer (kept in step under D-81) against NFR-04 / NFR-06, reported separately (never pooled), so the owner can confirm the preview exception or fall back to GA.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project, 004">Every tuned artefact is versioned: a new analyzer file and name, an Action JPS version bump; never an in-place change of a version already used for measured results or stored corrections.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-44">Baseline first, then tune; report both. Same item set and scoring rules across runs; the evaluation set is not edited to improve a score.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-06, FR-26">Settings changes from 161 are applied in dev only through the admin form (audited) and re-measured against NFR-06 before keeping them.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-01, NFR-02">p90 measured on at least 20 runs per surface at the spec sizes (invoices up to 20 pages / 150 lines), with the largest evaluation items included; timings recorded with run ids.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-015">Results contain ids, counts, rates and timings — no real-document text, names or amounts.</constraint>
    <constraint source=".claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md">If any src/server/api file changes (performance fix or defect), BFF hygiene applies: publish-size delta against a fresh master build, no new HIGH CVE, code-review; otherwise record "no BFF change".</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/ebilling-r1/spec.md (FR-44, NFR-01 – NFR-06, Success Criteria)</file>
      <file>projects/ebilling-r1/notes/calibration-report.md</file>
      <file>projects/ebilling-r1/notes/extraction-spike.md</file>
      <file>.claude/skills/jps-action-create/SKILL.md</file>
      <file>.claude/skills/jps-validate/SKILL.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Baseline: run the full evaluation set through dev with current versions; score NFR-04 / 05 / 06 with the 005 / 161 harnesses; measure NFR-01 and NFR-02 p90.</step>
    <step order="1">Diagnose misses per field and per code set (misread vs misresolved vs miscoded); list candidate changes with expected effect and cost.</step>
    <step order="2">Tune in this order, re-measuring after each: settings from 161; code-set mappings and chunk size; Action prompt versions (jps-validate before seeding); analyzer v2 (Deploy-Analyzers.ps1 -WhatIf then real; then set App Service setting ContentUnderstanding__AnalyzerId on spaarke-bff-dev — section from 003 / 043; record the name, not secrets). If 005 was no-go, tune the fallback extraction Action version instead of an analyzer.</step>
    <step order="3">Performance: if p90 misses, profile the stage timings in the job status (049) and the page network waterfall; fix in scope or file via /project-defer-issue-tracking.</step>
    <step order="4">Write notes/evaluation-results.md: method, item counts, baseline and tuned tables per NFR, versions measured, changes kept and rejected, cost per invoice.</step>
    <step order="5">For any target still missed: raise the escalation, record the owner decision as a D-entry in notes/decisions-log.md, and reference it in the results.</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md: this task's status cell to "✅ [done]".</step>
    <step order="7">Record deviations in projects/ebilling-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If any of NFR-01, NFR-02, NFR-04, NFR-05 or NFR-06 is still missed after tuning, STOP and raise 🔔 Human Input Required with the measured value, the gap, options (accept for R1 with a follow-up issue; further tuning with estimated effort and cost; scope change such as more review flags) and a recommendation. Record the owner's decision; never mark the target met.</trigger>
    <trigger>If a tuning change would require changing a version already referenced by stored correction records, STOP — create a new version instead.</trigger>
    <trigger>If evaluation runs would exceed the cost the owner accepted in 005 / 161, STOP and agree a budget.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>sprk-invoice-v1.json (004) and the eBilling Action mirrors; Deploy-Analyzers.ps1 and Deploy-ActionMirrors.ps1 deploy them.</existing>
    <extension>A tuned analyzer cannot edit v1 in place: 004's rule and the stored correction versions require a new versioned file; Actions are versioned in place by their JPS version field.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without a new version, measured results and stored corrections could not be tied to the definition that produced them, breaking the D-47 / D-64 per-version analysis.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="pwsh">Deploy-Analyzers.ps1, Deploy-ActionMirrors.ps1, harnesses</tool>
    <tool name="dataverse-mcp">read_query; settings verification</tool>
    <tool name="ui-test">NFR-02 timing in dev</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="docs">projects/ebilling-r1/notes/evaluation-results.md</output>
    <output type="config">sprk-invoice-v2.json and Action version bumps, only if tuned</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Per D-69, report whether the provisional confidence weights and caps (sprk_ebillingsetting) meet NFR-04 - NFR-06 and recommend values for owner confirmation at UAT (163).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">evaluation-results.md reports baseline and tuned values for NFR-04 (header fields; line date, timekeeper, hours, rate, amount), NFR-05, NFR-06, NFR-01 p90 and NFR-02 p90, each with item or run count and the analyzer, Action and settings versions measured.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Every target is either met in the tuned run or has an owner decision D-entry in notes/decisions-log.md referenced from the results.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Every tuned artefact has a new version; no measured version was modified in place (git diff of earlier analyzer and Action files shows no content change other than a version bump).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The evaluation item set and scoring rules are identical between baseline and tuned runs.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Publish-size delta measured against a fresh master build and recorded in task notes if any BFF file changed (otherwise "no BFF change"); no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Success criterion 8 is verified by evaluation-results.md. Action rows need no solution-source edit (the infra/dataverse mirrors are the source). Record every version and setting name changed in dev for 163's UAT baseline.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Load the knowledge files first. Follow task-execute for the pre-execution checklist.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
